change:
  id: CHG-029
  title: A live proposer fills a generation, and every candidate's AgentUsage is recorded
  status: proposed
  intent: Fill a generation from the live model proposer rather than the fixture proposer, and record each candidate's observed agent usage in the journal and the experiment ledger with unobserved fields recorded as unavailable, which ADR-0006 names as slice 0 and ADR-0002 as the missing piece of Layer 1.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - ADR-0002
    - ADR-0006
    - ARCH-001
    - CON-002
    - Q-013
    - PAT-004
    - RISK-007

deltas:
  - op: ADDED
    capability: mutation-fitness-loop
    requirement: A generation can be filled by the live model proposer. The proposer is asked for each variant explicitly, so the N asks are distinguishable to the model and each answer arrives as its own observable request.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: a generation of N candidates is requested with the live proposer profile
        then: the proposer is asked for variant k explicitly, and the variant marker is observable in the request that goes to the model
        and:
          - LangChain4jMutationProposalAdapter overrides the two single-argument entry points only (LangChain4jMutationProposalAdapter.java:67-79), so the variant-aware default ignores the variant (MutationProposer.java:29-34) and a generation asks the model the identical question N times. Q-013 records that the variant number never reaches the prompt
          - the only proposer that overrides the variant entry point today is the fixture (FixtureMutationProposer.java:72)
          - asking is not checking: the prompt carries the variant so the model can vary, and the sameness rule in S3 is what enforces that it did. The acceptance stub answers only requests whose body carries the variant marker, so a proposer that never sends it fails the test rather than passing on a canned answer
      - id: S2
        when: the live proposer returns N distinct variants for a generation
        then: the generation evaluates, ranks and records all N exactly as the fixture-filled path does, with each candidate's branch, worktree and fitness row produced by the existing per-candidate wiring
        and:
          - EvolveRunner builds one MutationEvaluationLoop per candidate position and delegates the variant through VariantProposer (EvolveRunner.java:224-235 and EvolveRunner.java:385-408); nothing about that wiring is fixture-specific, so the live profile composes onto it unchanged
          - this is the ADR-0002 Layer-1 gap closing: the variety a generation ranks stops being the fixture proposer padding its own canned mutation, which CHG-026 recorded as the thing its spread could not show

  - op: MODIFIED
    capability: mutation-fitness-loop
    requirement: A generation still refuses to rank one mutation against itself, but decides sameness on the pair (mutation id, patch) rather than on the id alone, so a live proposer that reuses a free-text id over genuinely different patches is ranked rather than failed with a half-true diagnosis. This settles Q-013.
    scenarios:
      - id: S3
        when: two candidates in a generation carry the same mutation id and the same patch
        then: the run fails and the failure names non-variation as the cause, because the diagnosis is now exactly true
        and:
          - today the comparison is on the id alone (GenerationEvaluationLoop.java:100-112) and its own message says a same-id-different-patch case would be failed with a diagnosis that is only half true
          - the mutation must reach the rule: GenerationEvaluationLoop sees only FitnessResult (GenerationEvaluationLoop.java:63-64), and FitnessResult carries the Candidate and not the Mutation that produced it (FitnessResult.java:6-16), so the per-candidate evaluation return widens to carry the Mutation alongside the result
          - the failure still leaves the per-candidate fitness rows of what was evaluated and no generation row, which is correct: a generation that cannot be ranked was never a comparison
      - id: S4
        when: two candidates in a generation carry the same mutation id over different patches
        then: both are evaluated and ranked, because a model-chosen id is a hint and the patch is the substance
        and:
          - the rule stays a hard check rather than trust in the prompt: the variant ask of S1 exists so the model can comply, and this rule exists because compliance is never assumed, which is the same division the port documents at MutationProposer.java:24-27
          - identity derived from the realised tree rather than the proposal remains the recorded destination, the same instinct as the declared-locus gate, and is not built here

  - op: MODIFIED
    capability: mutation-fitness-loop
    requirement: AgentUsage declares per-field availability at the harness boundary. Each consumption field - input tokens, output tokens, credits, wall clock, retries - is optional, empty means unobserved, and a present zero means a measured zero, so a placeholder zero can no longer masquerade as a measurement anywhere the value travels. The value also carries an optional price identity (provider, model), because cost is comparable only between attempts whose price identity is known.
    scenarios:
      - id: S8
        when: a candidate is proposed through the harness path and the harness reports its usage
        then: fields the harness measured and fields it did not are distinguishable in the recorded observation, even when their raw numbers are equal
        and:
          - AgentUsage today has primitive fields only (AgentUsage.java:7-26), so AcpAgentHarness's placeholder zeros for tokens and credits (AcpAgentHarness.java:72,83) are indistinguishable from a measured zero, and no translation downstream can recover the difference
          - the fix is at the boundary, not in a translator: AgentRunResult keeps carrying AgentUsage (AgentRunResult.java:13), but each field declares its own availability, AcpAgentHarness declares wall clock measured and the rest unavailable, and MutationProposerAgentHarness declares everything unavailable (it wraps a local proposer; nothing is invoked)
          - the test uses equal raw values with different availability - a measured zero against an unobserved field - which the primitive shape cannot express and the per-field shape must record differently
          - price identity is recorded only when observed. On the openai-compatible path it is the model the provider's response declares, which S5 covers. On the harness path it is NULL: AgentRoute records "intent, not provider proof" (AgentRoute.java:3) and the ACP route's model is the literal "configured" (ProposerProfileRegistry.java:40-43), so copying it would write a placeholder as a price identity

  - op: ADDED
    capability: mutation-fitness-loop
    requirement: Every evaluated candidate's observed agent usage is recorded in the journal and the experiment ledger, keyed to its candidate. A field the proposer did not observe is recorded as unavailable, never as zero, because a zero is a measurement claim and an unobserved price must never be estimated.
    scenarios:
      - id: S5
        when: a candidate proposed by the live proposer finishes its evaluation
        then: the ledger holds a usage row keyed to that candidate, carrying the provider and model it was proposed under as its price identity, the token counts the provider returned, the wall clock the adapter measured, and NULL for credits, which no chat-completions response reports
        and:
          - usage exists today only as unparsed strings in the candidate bookkeeping file inside the candidate worktree (LangChain4jMutationProposalAdapter.java:107-112) and as AgentUsage values the harness-path proposer discards (AgentHarnessMutationProposer.java:85); neither reaches the journal (JournalReporter.java:113-146) nor the ledger, whose migrations 1 to 3 carry no usage (SqliteExperimentMetadataStore.java:179-313)
          - the price identity has a real source: OpenAiCompatibleMutationProposerFactory passes only the literal profile id today (OpenAiCompatibleMutationProposerFactory.java:17-23) and the adapter holds no route or model, so the configured model name is threaded from the ModelEndpointConfig the factory already loads (ModelEndpointConfig.java:3, OpenAiCompatibleChatModelFactory.java:21-27) into the adapter and onto the observation. The recorded model is the one the provider's response declares, not the one requested; the WireMock stub declares a model name different from the configured one, and the test asserts the declared name, so copying the request instead fails
          - the channel must survive the per-candidate wiring: EvolveRunner.VariantProposer forwards proposerEvidence() today (EvolveRunner.java:404-407) and would not forward a new accessor unless made to, which would silently record unavailable for every live candidate; a wrapper-delegation test pins it
          - the asserted values are distinctive per variant, so a write that recorded a constant, the first candidate's values for everyone, or zeros would fail the test rather than pass on key presence
      - id: S6
        when: one variant's response carries usage and the next variant's response omits it
        then: the second candidate's usage row exists with its unobserved fields NULL, and does not inherit the first candidate's counts
        and:
          - this is a live defect today, not a hypothetical: AuditingChatModel sets the token fields only when tokenUsage() is non-null and never clears them (LangChain4jMutationProposalAdapter.java:220-228), so a no-usage response inherits the previous call's counts into the candidate bookkeeping; persisted, that leak would become durable audit data
          - the channel therefore clears captured state at the start of every invocation, and the test is two-variant on purpose: variant one's distinctive usage followed by variant two's absent usage is the order that catches the bleed, and variant one's row is asserted too so the bleed has something to be caught against
          - AGENTS.md requires recording unavailable rather than estimating an unsupported price, and ADR-0006 repeats it for routing evidence (docs/decisions/0006-budget-aware-harness-optimisation.md, decision 4); the run completes either way, because missing telemetry is not a candidate failure
          - the migration-3 precedent is the same shape: the generation spread is nullable because inventing a zero would read as a finding rather than an absence (SqliteExperimentMetadataStore.java:263-268)
      - id: S7
        when: a generation is run with the fixture proposer, which makes no model invocation at all
        then: every candidate's usage row exists with every field NULL - usage and price identity alike - rather than as zeros or placeholder names
        and:
          - the fixture profile constructs FixtureMutationProposer directly (ProposerProfileRegistry.java:37-38), not through MutationProposerAgentHarness, so nothing ever invokes a model for it; with the default-empty channel accessor the proposer simply has nothing to report, and unavailable is the only honest record
          - the test runs an actual --profile fixture generation and asserts one candidate_usage row per candidate with every field NULL, because a store that wrote AgentUsage.none() zeros (AgentUsage.java:24-26) or a placeholder provider would look identical to a correct write unless NULL is asserted explicitly
      - id: S9
        when: a candidate's journal entry is written
        then: the entry carries the candidate's observed usage fields and renders unobserved fields as unavailable
        and:
          - the journal is the narrative surface and the ledger is the audit record (JournalReporter.java:20-26); a person reading why a generation cost what it cost should not have to open a database
          - wall-clock values are asserted present, never asserted positive, because a fast stub can legitimately complete inside zero milliseconds and a positive-clock assertion would be flaky rather than wrong

