tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: AgentUsage redefined with per-field availability - each consumption field optional (empty means unobserved, present zero means measured zero, present values reject negatives exactly as AgentUsage does today at AgentUsage.java:14-22) plus an optional price identity of provider and model. AgentRunResult keeps carrying it (AgentRunResult.java:13), so availability is declared at the harness boundary and the placeholder-zero defect class is closed at construction. AcpAgentHarness declares wall clock measured and the rest unavailable; MutationProposerAgentHarness declares everything unavailable. Includes the equal-raw-values-different-availability domain test (S8)
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: the usage channel - a default-empty accessor on MutationProposer following the proposerEvidence precedent (MutationProposer.java:36-38), and an explicit requirement that EvolveRunner.VariantProposer forwards it exactly as it forwards proposerEvidence() (EvolveRunner.java:404-407), pinned by a wrapper-delegation test whose fixture reports a distinctive usage and fails if the wrapper drops the accessor (S5)
    status: completed
  - id: T3
    slice: the adapters populate the channel - LangChain4jMutationProposalAdapter reports tokens when the provider returns them, wall clock measured around the call, credits and retries unavailable, and a price identity whose model is the one the provider's response declares (NULL when it declares none). The configured model is threaded from ModelEndpointConfig (ModelEndpointConfig.java:3, OpenAiCompatibleChatModelFactory.java:21-27) through OpenAiCompatibleMutationProposerFactory (OpenAiCompatibleMutationProposerFactory.java:17-23) only so a requested/reported mismatch is visible in the journal; it is never written as the price identity. AuditingChatModel clears its captured state at the start of every invocation, closing the stale-token leak (S6). AgentHarnessMutationProposer forwards AgentRunResult.usage unchanged, availability now explicit at the source (S8), with no price identity, because its route is intent rather than observation
    status: pending
  - id: T4
    slice: the ledger record, standalone - migration 4 adding candidate_usage (provider, model, per-field NULL for unavailable, credits as exact decimal text), an abstract recordUsage on the ExperimentMetadataStore port following the recordGeneration precedent (ExperimentMetadataStore.java:12-18), the SQLite implementation, and direct integration tests writing and reading rows (S5 integration). Nothing consumes it yet, which is what makes it independently green
    status: pending
  - id: T5
    slice: the wiring - MutationEvaluationLoop reads the channel and writes usage beside the fitness row (MutationEvaluationLoop.java:237), the reporter callback, the journal's per-candidate usage line (S9), the loop-level store-and-reporter unit test (S5 unit) and the actual --profile fixture generation acceptance that pins one all-NULL row per candidate (S7)
    status: pending
  - id: T6
    slice: Q-013 settled in code - the per-candidate evaluation return carries the Mutation that produced it, and GenerationEvaluationLoop compares (id, patch): same id with same patch fails naming non-variation, same id with different patches ranks (S3, S4, unit and WireMock acceptance). The single-candidate MutationEvaluationLoop.evaluate signature is preserved for its current callers. Independent of T2 to T5 and may land before or after them
    status: pending
  - id: T7
    slice: the live fill - LangChain4jMutationProposalAdapter overrides the variant entry point and puts the variant into the model prompt (S1, S2), with the WireMock acceptance for a filled generation, for usage recorded from per-variant stubs (S5 acceptance) and for the two-variant stale-state guard (S6 acceptance)
    status: pending
  - id: T8
    slice: knowledge and documentation in the same change - Q-013 marked answered with the recommendation and the surviving alternative, ADR-0006 slice 0 noted as delivered, and HANDOFF, README and wiki updated where they name this gap
    status: pending

non_goals:
  - harness profiles, deterministic profile selection and progressive escalation, which are ADR-0006 slices A to C and each need their own change
  - any routing, learned or otherwise; Q-010 stays open and this slice produces evidence it will consume
  - cost per successful task, Pareto comparison and any cross-candidate cost aggregation, which are ADR-0006 slice F; generation-level totals are derivable from the per-candidate rows by a join
  - credit or price estimation of any kind: an unobserved field is recorded as unavailable, never estimated
  - variant-aware prompting for the ACP harness proposer. AgentHarnessMutationProposer keeps the default variant behaviour; its usage forwarding lands here, its generation-filling does not, and the openai-compatible profile is the one live proposer this slice fills
  - parallel candidate evaluation. The usage channel shares the proposerEvidence shape, which is sound only because evaluation is sequential (GenerationEvaluationLoop.java:14-18); parallelism would have to move usage onto the returned value and is its own change
  - usage of a proposal whose candidate was never created, for example a validation failure after the model answered; those tokens are consumed and currently unrecorded, which is recorded as an open question rather than silently scoped out
  - migration of ledger rows written before this change; the experiment ledger is derived data and is rebuilt, as with earlier schema changes
  - trace or corpus ingestion, which is ADR-0006 slice E

risks:
  - The variant ask trusts the model to vary, and the (id, patch) check is what enforces that it did. A model that answers every variant with the same id and the same patch fails the run loudly, by design, and the failure message names non-variation. The residual trust is that a model varying only its ids over identical patches now ranks N identical candidates; that is the realised-tree identity Q-013 records as the destination and this slice deliberately does not build.
  - The usage channel is per-candidate latest-proposal state, exactly as proposerEvidence already is (LangChain4jMutationProposalAdapter.java:97-118 reads the auditing model's last exchange). It is sound only under sequential evaluation; the non-goal on parallelism exists so that assumption cannot erode unnoticed. The AuditingChatModel stale-state defect (S6) is what this shape does when it is done carelessly, and the per-invocation clearing in T3 plus the two-variant test is the standing guard.
  - A default-empty accessor plus a wrapper that forgets to forward it is a silent all-unavailable record for every live candidate - the absence of evidence masquerading as evidence of absence. T2 names VariantProposer's delegation an explicit requirement and pins it with a test whose fixture reports a distinctive usage, so a non-delegating wrapper fails.
  - S1 could pass for the wrong reason if the stub answered any request: the acceptance stub matches the request body for the variant marker, following the existing body-matching precedent (EvolveCommandAcceptanceTest.java:574-603), so a proposer that never sends the marker gets no answer and the run fails.
  - S5 could pass for the wrong reason if the assertion checked row presence or any token count: the stub returns distinctive per-variant token counts and the test asserts each candidate's row equals its own variant's values, so a constant write, a first-candidate-wins write or a zero write fails. Credits are asserted NULL, not merely unasserted, and the model column is asserted equal to the model the stub's response declares, which differs from the configured name, so a placeholder or a copied request fails.
  - S6 could pass for the wrong reason as a single-candidate test, because an empty store has nothing to inherit from: it is a two-variant test in which variant one carries distinctive usage and variant two none, and both rows are asserted - variant two's NULLs prove the absence was recorded, variant one's values prove the bleed had something to be caught against.
  - S3's failure assertion pins the reason, not only the non-zero exit, because any failure - an unmatched stub, a validation rejection - would otherwise satisfy it; the message must name the repeated id and that the patch matched.
  - S4 must assert the ranking rows exist in the ledger, not only exit zero, because a generation that quietly dropped the second candidate would otherwise pass.
  - S7 guards the placeholder-to-zero confusion at the profile that never invokes a model: the fixture profile constructs FixtureMutationProposer directly (ProposerProfileRegistry.java:37-38), so the test asserts every field NULL on a real --profile fixture generation, and a store that persisted AgentUsage.none() zeros or a placeholder provider fails.
  - S8 guards the measured-zero/unavailable confusion that primitive fields made inexpressible: the test uses equal raw values with different availability and asserts they are recorded differently.
  - S9 never asserts a positive wall clock; a fast WireMock stub can complete inside zero milliseconds and a positive-clock assertion would be flaky rather than wrong.
  - The per-candidate evaluation return widening touches CandidateEvaluator, which the single-candidate path also uses (EvolveRunner.java:121-127); the existing single-candidate tests and the CHG-026 acceptance suite are the regression net, and the widening preserves the MutationEvaluationLoop.evaluate signature its current callers use.
  - Redefining AgentUsage touches every harness adapter construction in the same commit (T1), because a record's components are checked at compile time; that is the intended blast radius and it is what closes the placeholder-zero class rather than translating around it.
  - A generation filled by a live model costs real tokens per candidate even under a stubbed endpoint in tests; the acceptance tests run only against WireMock and no test may require a real provider.
